# Caddyfile for CoreMind Hub (Mac Mini)
#
# CoreMind Hub binds to 127.0.0.1:8765 by default. Caddy listens on all
# interfaces (:8765) and allows only loopback + Tailscale clients;
# everyone else gets 403.
#
# Why listen on :8765 instead of binding the Tailscale IP?
#   - No boot race: binding a specific Tailscale IP fails if Caddy starts
#     before Tailscale is up. ":8765" always binds.
#   - On macOS, Caddy's wildcard bind coexists with the Hub's 127.0.0.1
#     bind on the same port (local connections go straight to the Hub,
#     remote connections go through Caddy).
#   - NOTE: this pattern is macOS-only. On Linux the overlapping bind
#     fails with "address already in use" — the Pi's Caddyfile
#     (Caddyfile.node.example) uses an interface bind instead.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Install Caddy: brew install caddy
#   2. Run: caddy run --config Caddyfile.hub.example
#      (or: brew services start caddy — see docs/setup-hub.md)
#
# The allowlist admits the whole Tailscale range (100.64.0.0/10).
# To restrict to specific devices, list their IPs instead:
#   @allowed remote_ip 127.0.0.1 ::1 100.x.x.x 100.y.y.y

:8765 {
    @allowed remote_ip 127.0.0.1 ::1 100.64.0.0/10

    handle @allowed {
        reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8765
    }

    respond "Forbidden" 403
}
